    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet within one of Greystones' most exclusive residential enclaves off New Road, around the corner from the harbour, this truly exceptional A-rated four-bedroom semi-detached residence represents the very pinnacle of contemporary family living. Extending to an impressive 183 sq m / 1,970 sq ft approx, the property was acquired new in 2024 and has since been extensively enhanced with an extraordinary level of bespoke finishes, creating a home of remarkable sophistication, style and comfort. Built by the highly regarded Durkan Homes, every detail has been carefully considered, resulting in a turnkey residence of outstanding quality.\n\nBehind its attractive façade lies light-filled interiors where beautifully proportioned accommodation with soaring ceiling heights and exquisite craftsmanship combine seamlessly, while a carefully curated palette of luxurious materials creates a calm and cohesive aesthetic. Hardwood flooring extends across the entire ground floor, while sumptuous plush carpeting provides exceptional comfort throughout the upper levels. The elegant sitting room offers an inviting retreat, distinguished by bespoke cabinetry with slimline TV set within, and striking timber wall panelling that continues through the hall, staircase, landing and principal bedroom suite, adding warmth, texture and architectural interest throughout the home. Window coverings, including bespoke plantation shutters and high end double lined curtains create an intimate atmosphere of refined finish. \n\nThe heart of the home is an outstanding open-plan kitchen, dining and family room where expansive glazing (with floor to ceiling double lined curtains) frames views of the beautifully landscaped rear garden. The superbly appointed contemporary kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of bespoke cabinetry, premium Siemens integrated appliances and generous quartz worktops, creating a space equally suited to everyday family living and entertaining. The adjoining light filled living area, with acoustic timber slat wall panelling and wall mounted smart TV, flows seamlessly to the sun-drenched patio and professionally landscaped gardens beyond.\n\nThe bedroom accommodation is equally impressive, comprising four generous double bedrooms arranged over two upper floors. The luxurious principal suite occupies the second floor, offering a dual-aspect peaceful sanctuary complete with bespoke panelled detailing, extensive fitted wardrobes & eaves storage and a beautifully appointed en-suite bathroom. A second en-suite bedroom, together with two further spacious double bedrooms and a stylish family bathroom, ensures the home is perfectly suited to modern family living.\n\nThe high-end finishes continue throughout, complemented by a state-of-the-art Vent-Axia ventilation system, energy-efficient A-rated performance and a rarely rivalled impeccable standard of presentation.\n\nOutside, the beautifully landscaped rear garden provides a private and tranquil retreat, perfectly designed for both relaxation and entertaining. The location is equally compelling, with the vibrant heart of Greystones, renowned schools, coastal amenities, shops, cafés, the marina and DART all within easy reach. Combining an enviable address, exceptional specification and effortless convenience, this is a truly outstanding home that sets a benchmark for luxury living in Greystones."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA wide entrance with hardwood flooring, high ceilings, wall panelling, recessed downlighting. Alarm panel. Access to understairs cloaks storage.\n\nSitting Room: - 3.73m x 6.11m\nPart glazed door opens to front facing reception, with built in downlit cabinetry holding slimline TV, antique brass power and light switches, recessed downlighting, plantation shutters and Helen Turkington double lined curtains.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 5.87m x 6.00m\nA dual aspect open plan space with hardwood flooring, wall mounted smart TV set upon contemporary acoustic timber slat wall panelling, recessed downlighting, 2 skylights and large glazed sliding doors opening to landscaped rear garden. Cream floor and eye level kitchen units, quartz counter tops and splashback, stainless steel sink and drainer, antique brass tap, power and light switches. Integrated appliances include American size fridge & freezer, Siemens induction hob, oven, microwave, dishwasher.\n\nUtility Room: - 1.78m x 1.59m\nTiled floor, provision for dryer, plumbed for washing machine. Stainless steel sink.\n\nGuest WC - 1.83m x 1.50m\nTiled floor, wall panelling, WC, wash hand basin with storage beneath & LED mirror above.\n\nFirst Floor - \nBright dual aspect landing with wall panelling and recessed downlighting.\n\nHot Press: - \n\n\nBedroom 2: - 3.69m x 3.58m\nA bright double to the front, with box bay window, plantation shutters and luxurious curtains, recessed downlighting and double built in wardrobes.\n\nEn-suite shower room - 2.69m x 1.41m\nTiled floor and shower with glazed door and luxurious waterfall and handheld showerheads. WC, wash hand basin with storage below and LED mirror above. Heated chrome towel rail, recessed downlighting.\n\nBedroom 3: - 2.86m x 4.10m\nLarge double to the rear with built in wardrobes and Roman blinds.\n\nBedroom 4: - 2.94m x 2.98m\nLaid out as a home office, with feature wall panelling, plantation shutters, built in wardrobes and overlooking rear garden.\n\nFamily Bathroom: - 1.80m x 2.66m\nTiled floor, heated chrome towel rail, tiled shower with glazed door and both waterfall and handheld attachments, Wash hand basin with built in storage below and LED wall mounted mirror above.\n\nSecond Floor: - \nLanding with skylight leading to:\n\nPrincipal Bedroom 1: - 4.76m x 8.07m\nSpanning the entire top floor, decorated in maritime tones, a dual aspect light filled space with plush curtains and bespoke wooden blinds, built in wardrobes and eaves storage.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.64m x 2.41m\nTiled floor, Velux window, recessed downlighting, heated chrome towel rail, wash hand basin with tiled splashback and LED mirror above, WC.\n\nGarden: - \nCobble block off-street car parking, gated side access to landscaped rear garden which has been designed to provide year-round structure with a primary palette of whites, greens and burgundy foliage. Along the rear border mature Birch trees give a high degree of privacy while the beds are brimming with white Petunia, Hydrangeas, a red Japanese Maple, Agapanthus, and evergreen climbing Hydrangea with Portuguese Laurel hedging. Two paved patio areas area one to follow the sun in this beautifully presented oasis of calm.\n\n"
      },
